nel's "},{"id":"spn-24051","marks":["bold"],"text":"resource"},{"id":"spn-24052","text":" rung — the affine ledger where a token is either "},{"id":"spn-24053","marks":["italic"],"text":"depletable"},{"id":"spn-24054","text":" (linear: consumed once) or "},{"id":"spn-24055","marks":["italic"],"text":"reusable"},{"id":"spn-24056","text":" (affine/\"of-course\": intact after use). "},{"id":"spn-24057","marks":["bold"],"text":"Recommendation:"},{"id":"spn-24058","text":" when V0.2 lands, name this correspondence explicitly and reuse the resource-rung vocabulary ("},{"id":"spn-24059","marks":["code"],"text":"consume"},{"id":"spn-24060","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24061","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-24062","text":" annihilation on overspend) rather than inventing a parallel one. The kernel's "},{"id":"spn-24063","marks":["code"],"text":"resource.mjs"},{"id":"spn-24064","text":" (laws "},{"id":"spn-24065","marks":["code"],"text":"C1–C8"},{"id":"spn-24066","text":", "},{"id":"spn-24067","marks":["code"],"text":"CB1–CB3"},{"id":"spn-24068","text":") is the reference semantics."}]},{"id":"blk-23187","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24069","text":"4. An optional \"verify\" gate is just an ordinary phase"}]},{"id":"blk-23188","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24070","text":"A loop that wants the kernel to gate a commit declares a normal "},{"id":"spn-24071","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-24072","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-24073","marks":["code"],"text":"act"},{"id":"spn-24074","text":" phase whose body calls "},{"id":"spn-24075","marks":["code"],"text":"bridge.select(...)"},{"id":"spn-24076","text":". PULSE needs "},{"id":"spn-24077","marks":["bold"],"text":"no new phase kind"},{"id":"spn-24078","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-24079","marks":["bold"],"text":"no schema change"},{"id":"spn-24080","text":" — the verdict is a phase "},{"id":"spn-24081","marks":["italic"],"text":"body"},{"id":"spn-24082","text":", and its result is an ordinary "},{"id":"spn-24083","marks":["code"],"text":"OutcomeSignal"},{"id":"spn-24084","text":" (or a "},{"id":"spn-24085","marks":["code"],"text":"DeliberationResult"},{"id":"spn-24086","text":" when κ>0). Keep the 5 canonical phase kinds intact."}]},{"id":"blk-23189","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24087","text":"What this review deliberately does NOT do"}]},{"id":"blk-23190","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23192","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24088","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-24089","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-24090","text":" add an 8th invariant, a verdict phase kind, or any required field — the"}]}],"id":"blk-23191","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24091","text":"v0.1 schema is unchanged and remains backward compatible."}]},{"id":"blk-23194","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24092","text":"It does "},{"id":"spn-24093","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-24094","text":" claim a rung↔phase-kind bijection (the two are orthogonal axes)."}]}],"id":"blk-23195","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24095","text":"Enforcement of the deontic/strategic/reflexive rungs stays in the runtime that "},{"id":"spn-24096","marks":["italic"],"text":"hosts"}]}],"id":"blk-23197","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24097","text":"the loop (Delegatic for policy/audit), not in the manifest."}]},{"id":"blk-23200","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-24098","text":"Follow-ups (out of scope here)"}]},{"id":"blk-23201","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-24099","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-24100","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-conformance"},{"id":"spn-24101","text":" checker that lifts "},{"id":"spn-24102","marks":["code"],"text":"invariants"},{"id":"spn-24103","text":" → 